"name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518733,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","color":"447744","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-22T07:07:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T08:43:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested versions:\n4.6.3\n\nThe issue was also present in previous 4.6.x versions and in 4.5.x versions\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11, Godot v4.6.3.stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using Remote Scene Tree \"Select Mode\" during runtime debugging, a fullscreen transparent ColorRect is still selected by the picker even if its Mouse Filter is set to Ignore.\n\nThis makes it difficult to inspect nodes behind fullscreen UI overlays or autoload UI layers.\n\nThe issue appears to affect editor picking behavior only. Gameplay input behaves correctly.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\nCreate a fullscreen ColorRect inside a Control/CanvasLayer.\nSet its color alpha to 0 (fully transparent).\nSet Mouse > Filter = Ignore.\nRun the project.\nEnable Remote Scene Tree Select Mode.\nTry selecting nodes behind the ColorRect.\n\nExpected result:\nThe picker should ignore the ColorRect and select nodes behind it.\n\nActual result:\nThe picker still selects the fullscreen ColorRect.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119649/reactions","total_count":0